# Bioloop Project Rules for AI Agents

## ⚠️ PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT WARNINGS

**THIS IS THE PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT.**

### Access Restrictions

You only have access to:
- `/opt/sca/cmg` on host `cmg-new-service1.sca.iu.edu` (contains current repository)
- `/opt/sca/cmg-bioloop` if it exists on the host (current repo path on other hosts)
- `/tmp` for temporary read/write/delete operations

### Critical Restrictions

- **NEVER EVER EVER** write/delete anything in paths beginning with `/N/...`
- **NEVER** reset the database yourself. Only do so if user explicitly permits in chat.
- **NEVER** exec into docker containers or restart them. Ask user and provide commands if needed.
- **ALWAYS** delete anything written to `/tmp` after work is done.
- You do **NOT** have sudo access in production.

### Host Restrictions

- You can only make changes on `cmg-new-service1.sca.iu.edu` (use hostname - it's in the allowlist)
- You don't have access to `/opt/sca/cmg` on any other host

